  "status": "PROVED SUFFICIENT SURPLUS BARRIER FOR X50",
  "task": "X55 h=4 surplus-threshold bridge",
  "theorem": "Let T(n) be the X50 exact shell threshold.  X54 gives N_surplus >= n*C(M,2) for a quotient shell of size M.  Therefore N_surplus < n*C(T(n)+1,2) rules out M >= T(n)+1, hence M <= T(n), and X50 puts the centered h=4 branch inside the n^3 terminal column. This is a sufficient condition only.  The exact surplus barrier has room for a total-surplus bound at the 6*n^(5/3) scale on every recorded threshold row, checked by 216*n^2 < C(T+1,2)^3."
